<title>UK: SmithKline in two drug discovery tie-ups.</title>
<headline>SmithKline in two drug discovery tie-ups.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British pharmaceuticals group SmithKline Beecham Plc said on Thursday it had agreed two collaboration deals to improve its drug discovery potential.</p>
<p>SmithKline said it had agreed collaborations with Cadus Pharmaceutical Corporation of Tarrytown, N.Y., and with Evotec BioSystems GmbH of Hamburg, Germany.</p>
<p>SmithKline said the Cadus deal would augment its genomics expertise with Cadus' proprietary technology for the expression and functional coupling of human cellular receptors in yeast.</p>
<p>The Evotec deal would bring instrumentation and optical technology to suppport ultra-high throughput screening, SmithKline said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
